      "profile": "compound-v1: pre-allocation resource budget \u003c=4,000,000 conservative full-support axis taps: (scene_width_4x+scene_height_4x) * (ceil(6*max(1,1/(4*uniform_scale)))+1), including out-of-source normalization work; \u003c=32,000,000 retained weight bytes plus \u003c=32,000,000 temporary kernel bytes; reject before weights allocate. Uniform whole-source pixel-edge affine to full 4x scene; transparent extension; separable antialiased premultiplied byte-RGB Lanczos3, signed lobes, source-space radius widened by reduction, output-only rounding and existing alpha/color clamp policy. Outer union boundary formed by reciprocal edge cancellation; explicit reference-layout framing: preserve full affine source at the requested inset; report the eight-world-pixel boundary band diagnostically without rejection or fade. Existing resizeLanczos filters full unmasked 4x artwork to whole-scene 2x before final union clipping. Ground independently exported by exportConnectionTiles with fixed geometry and grass only, PNG decoded and assembled at exact tile origins; never sampled at scene origin. Compose artwork globally over actual ground PNG assembly, mask union only at final pixels; crop without filtering, final complementary top-left half-open ownership. Decode tile PNG bytes and reassemble ordinary image.Draw Over. Both runtime line parities use actual PNGs, ground first, compound second. Pixel-aligned 2x/4x only; no runtime/whole-map/user acceptance claim.",
